    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d201">

                <pb facs="0477" n="353" xml:id="pg353"/>

                <head>No. 201.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Dichman to Mr. Evarts</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-03-30"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 30, 1881</date>.
                        (Received May 6.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 258.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In compliance with the instructions
                    contained in your No. 149 of the 20th of last January, relating to the
                    protection afforded to Colombian citizens in Peru by the minister of the United
                    States at Lima, I addressed a note to the Colombian secretary of foreign
                    relations embodying the statements contained in your dispatch, and I am now in
                    receipt of an answer from that gentleman in which he makes due acknowledgment of
                    the friendly services of Mr. Christiancy, as well as expressing a proper
                    appreciation of the approval extended to his action by the Department.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>ERNEST DICHMAN.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d201-a1.xml" xpointer="d201-a1"/>
